    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78358" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραλληλ-ισμός</span></b> , ὁ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>false reasoning,
			fallacy</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς π. κατά τινων ποιήσονται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lycurg.
					31
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				11.465
			</span></i>, etc.; <i>false inference</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ θεάτρου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Po.</u>
					1455a13
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἔξω τῆς λέξεως π</span>.
			material <i>fallacies</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ παρὰ
				τὴν λέξιν ἔλεγχοι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>SE</u>
				166b21
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>weakness of reasoning power</i>, Aristeas <i><span class="en">
				250
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>deception, fraud</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.81.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PLond.</u>
				1.24.26
			</span></i><span class="entity">(ii B. C.)</span>, etc.</div>
